Subject: [PATCH 9/9] docs: T12 gets the evaluation flags, the measured widths,
 and a three-row table

Three of evaluate_hybrid_policy's defaults disagree with how this round trains
-- horizon 20 against 35, radial_local against arrival_condition, and
phase/time observation off while training sets it on -- and the third is a
refused load rather than a quiet mismatch. Section 4 now spells all three out,
points at the manifest's evaluation_flags line, and carries a full command that
was actually run in the sandbox: train, write final_model.zip, load it back
through the dimension check and step episodes.

Section 3's observation widths were my arithmetic rather than a measurement and
were wrong: arrival_condition is 32D and radial_local 31D, because train_hybrid
turns the phase/time observation on unconditionally, so neither is the bare
24-plus-ratchet I wrote. A wrong width there sends the lower window to the
wrong loader flags.

Pure SAC drops out of this round's table on the upper window's call -- three
rows now, with that row deferred until the coupling line is clean.

